{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":1560,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"This domain is found in glutamate synthase, tungsten formylmethanofuran dehydrogenase subunit c (FwdC) and molybdenum formylmethanofuran dehydrogenase subunit c (FmdC). A repeated G-XX-G-XXX-G motif is seen in the alignment.","domain_architectures":158,"interpro_id":"IPR002489","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":21244,"name":"GXGXG motif","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF01493","proteins":21023,"proteomes":17485,"short_name":"GXGXG","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF01493","structures":13,"taxa":27304,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-direct-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","history":[{"action":"CREATE","agent":"Codex","curator":"Codex","description":"Read Cottevieille 2008 main and supplemental evidence; inspected DLS Figure S3, kinetic Table 2 and construction pages. Mapped the exact deposited mature sequence to Q05755, resolving the 36-residue offset and partial-domain delta40 deletion. Retained two direct salt/particle-size effects and one indirect reported expression phenotype; no isolated-domain sufficiency or direct folding claim. Complete clones, nucleotide-coordinate prose and physiological contexts remain unresolved. IN_PROGRESS; no publication.","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF01493/2026-10-11T105840Z-codex-e03f25.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"local_source":"source/history/records/PF01493/2026-10-11T105840Z-codex-e03f25.yaml","outcome":"changed","source_path":"history/records/PF01493/2026-10-11T105840Z-codex-e03f25.yaml","summary":"Curated scoped GltS assembly and truncation graphs for PF01493.","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:58:40Z","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/42221c55a429e9d34b7bbb00704b24ff01313542/history/records/PF01493/2026-10-11T105840Z-codex-e03f25.yaml"},{"action":"REVIEW","agent":"Codex","curator":"Codex","description":"Assessed the current three-edge projection and primary evidence, including visual recheck of supplemental DLS plots. Verified native projection and overlay agreement. Two direct size effects and one indirect production phenotype remain supported with explicit construct, domain and assay limitations. Saved NEEDS_FOLLOWUP review; complete family coverage and isolated-domain mechanisms remain open. No status promotion or publication.","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF01493/2026-10-11T110713Z-codex-6f6ef9.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"local_source":"source/history/records/PF01493/2026-10-11T110713Z-codex-6f6ef9.yaml","outcome":"needs_followup","source_path":"history/records/PF01493/2026-10-11T110713Z-codex-6f6ef9.yaml","summary":"Retained partial GltS assembly and expression scientific self-review.","timestamp":"2026-10-11T11:07:13Z","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/42221c55a429e9d34b7bbb00704b24ff01313542/history/records/PF01493/2026-10-11T110713Z-codex-6f6ef9.yaml"}],"local_source":"source/data/families/PF01493.yaml","record":{"causal_graphs":[{"context":"Compare 1 mg/ml GltSHis after 17 h at 15 C with 1 M added NaCl or no added NaCl in 25 mM HEPES/KOH pH 7.5, 1 mM EDTA and 1 mM DTT. The plotted DLS radius is measured on the treated preparation. General DLS Methods describe a 50-ul cuvette and twenty 30-s acquisitions; these acquisitions are not independent preparations. The untagged enzyme is reported to behave similarly, but its unshown experiment is not a separate edge.","edges":[{"directness":"DIRECT","edge_id":"salt-decreases-gltshis-radius","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF01493/cottevieille-2008-assembly.txt","cache_sha256":"cb7d78a923b2aeb774855712227aa70f50c19af66cc12f781b33b86a04f17521","explanation":"Visually inspected supplemental Figure 3C and its caption on supplement page 9 establish the 17-h salt comparison; main enzyme Methods and supplemental DLS Methods define the preparation and measurement.","reference":"PMID:18199747","snippet":"calculated radius","source_url":"https://people.impmc.fr/sjonic/Papers/JBC_GltS.pdf"},{"cache_path":"evidence/PF01493/GltS-identity.txt","cache_sha256":"156cb20252c22d4a17437babc87c16b813dfc77aa7f714b724c9812b21276e1d","explanation":"Reference mapping and the exact 1EA0 sequence alignment distinguish the mature alpha-subunit numbering from precursor coordinates and from the partner beta subunit.","reference":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/Q05755/entry/pfam/PF01493/","snippet":"Q05755 Pfam:PF01493; domain interval: 1249-1496, inclusive.","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/Q05755/entry/pfam/PF01493/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"The 1-M-NaCl endpoint has a smaller measured particle radius than the matched no-added-salt preparation. The directly observed purified-complex effect is retained without equating the DLS readout with an atomically resolved PF01493 interface transition.","object":"gltshis-dls-radius","predicate":"decreases","subject":"gltshis-one-molar-nacl","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"Alpha-subunit reference UniProtKB:Q05755 is 1515 aa, sequence version 1; PF01493 spans 1249-1496. UniProt and InterPro sequences agree. PDB 1EA0 polymer 1-1479 exactly matches reference 37-1515, establishing the mature-protein offset of 36 and a mature-domain interval of 1213-1460. The tested complex retains the other alpha domains and beta partner. The reference sequence paper identifies Sp7, but the complete 2008 clones and original donor strain were not independently reconstructed.","graph_id":"azospirillum-glts-salt-radius","limitations":"DLS measures particle-size behavior, not domain-specific contact rupture or unique oligomer composition. SAXS and cryo-EM support an assembly interpretation but use separate measurements and mixture models. Some irreversible subunit loss and activity decrease occur on prolonged salt treatment. This is not salt-dependent cellular regulation, isolated-domain sufficiency or an observed electron-transfer trajectory.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:Q05755"],"label":"GltSHis incubated with 1 M added NaCl rather than no added NaCl for 17 h","node_id":"gltshis-one-molar-nacl","node_type":"PERTURBATION"},{"label":"DLS-derived radius of the purified GltSHis particles","node_id":"gltshis-dls-radius","node_type":"STATE"}],"scope":"Recombinant A. brasilense glutamate synthase containing wild-type alpha and C-terminally His6-tagged beta in Cottevieille 2008 Figure S3C; not an isolated GXGXG domain.","scope_status":"MECHANISTIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:192","title":"Added NaCl lowers the measured radius of purified GltSHis particles"},{"context":"A 1.2-mg/ml sample previously incubated for 17 h with 1 M NaCl is diluted tenfold into the same HEPES/EDTA/DTT buffer without NaCl. The matched control is diluted tenfold into buffer containing 1 M NaCl. Calculated final protein is 0.12 mg/ml in both; residual NaCl in the low-salt arm is 0.1 M, not zero. DLS follows radius over approximately 500 s using 10-s acquisitions. General DLS temperature is 15 C; the caption does not separately establish the pretreatment temperature for this panel.","edges":[{"directness":"DIRECT","edge_id":"low-salt-dilution-increases-radius","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF01493/cottevieille-2008-assembly.txt","cache_sha256":"cb7d78a923b2aeb774855712227aa70f50c19af66cc12f781b33b86a04f17521","explanation":"Visually inspected supplemental Figure 3D and its caption distinguish both dilution arms, the 17-h pretreatment, starting concentration and 10-s measurement interval. Supplemental Table 1 supplies separate reversibility context, not identical conditions.","reference":"PMID:18199747","snippet":"re-association","source_url":"https://people.impmc.fr/sjonic/Papers/JBC_GltS.pdf"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"The low-salt-dilution trace increases while the equal-dilution high-salt control remains near its starting size. The net reassembly-associated size change is observed in the purified preparation, without asserting which domain supplies an independently sufficient interface.","object":"post-dilution-gltshis-radius","predicate":"increases","subject":"salt-treated-gltshis-low-salt-dilution","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"Q05755 alpha contains PF01493 at precursor 1249-1496, corresponding to mature 1213-1460 after removal of residues 1-36. The exact deposited mature sequence matches the current reference. This assay uses intact alpha/beta complexes with beta, not alpha, carrying the His6 extension.","graph_id":"azospirillum-glts-salt-dilution-radius","limitations":"The two arms have matched dilution but different salt concentrations. Increased hydrodynamic size supports reassociation without proving exact stoichiometry, complete recovery, a unique GXGXG-mediated contact or a cellular mechanism. A fitted single-exponential curve and repeated acquisitions are not independent biological replications or an atomistic rate constant.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:Q05755"],"label":"Tenfold dilution of salt-treated GltSHis into NaCl-free buffer instead of 1-M-NaCl buffer","node_id":"salt-treated-gltshis-low-salt-dilution","node_type":"PERTURBATION"},{"label":"DLS-derived particle radius after dilution","node_id":"post-dilution-gltshis-radius","node_type":"STATE"}],"scope":"Purified wild-type-alpha/His6-beta GltSHis in Cottevieille 2008 Figure S3D; a separate dilution experiment, not full recovery of all original complexes.","scope_status":"MECHANISTIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:192","title":"Salt dilution increases particle radius after GltSHis salt treatment"},{"context":"pETGltSHis-derived T7 coproduction constructs encode either wild-type, delta7 or delta40 alpha. Supplemental Methods describe 30-C growth to absorbance about 2 followed by 25 C without IPTG, with delta40 attempts also using 25 C for 6-7 h or 15 C with 0.1 mM IPTG for 17 h. Delta7 production/purification is retained, whereas no truncated delta40 polypeptide production was observed. The main text compares with the productive full-length preparation. No plotted expression gel or detection threshold is supplied for delta40 in the inspected material.","edges":[{"directness":"INDIRECT","edge_id":"delta40-decreases-detectable-alpha","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF01493/cottevieille-2008-assembly.txt","cache_sha256":"cb7d78a923b2aeb774855712227aa70f50c19af66cc12f781b33b86a04f17521","explanation":"Main page 8245 and supplemental construction/expression Methods on pages 1-2 report the negative production result. The Methods and printed primers were visually checked; a delta40 protein gel was not independently available for assessment.","reference":"PMID:18199747","snippet":"no production","source_url":"https://people.impmc.fr/sjonic/Papers/JBC_GltS.pdf"},{"cache_path":"evidence/PF01493/GltS-identity.txt","cache_sha256":"156cb20252c22d4a17437babc87c16b813dfc77aa7f714b724c9812b21276e1d","explanation":"Exact sequence comparison and deposited alignment resolve the 36-residue numbering offset; only 21 deleted residues lie in the current Pfam interval.","reference":"https://files.rcsb.org/download/1EA0.cif","snippet":"The deposited 1EA0 polymer is exactly Q05755 residues 37-1515.","source_url":"https://files.rcsb.org/download/1EA0.cif"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"The source reports no detectable production of the delta40 alpha polypeptide across the attempted expression conditions, unlike the productive full-length and delta7 constructs. The observed expression outcome is indirect with respect to folding or assembly and is not converted into a uniquely resolved molecular mechanism.","object":"detectable-alpha-polypeptide","predicate":"decreases","subject":"gltb-delta40-coproduction","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"Q05755 precursor 37-1515 matches mature 1EA0 residues 1-1479. The delta40 deletion maps to precursor 1476-1515, overlapping PF01493 at 1476-1496 and also removing an outside-domain tail. Reverse-complement translation of printed Oligo 3 ends at reference EEHVTETQSRF, residues 1465-1475, followed by two stops. Delta7 removes 1509-1515 outside PF01493; Oligo 2 locally matches the retained terminus. Printed nucleotide stop-position prose does not fully agree with this mapping; whole clones remain unverified.","graph_id":"azospirillum-glts-delta40-expression","limitations":"This is a reported negative production endpoint in a heterologous host, not a direct protein-folding, degradation or translation assay. Detection method, quantitative limits, independent clone counts and rescue are not established. The authors' exposed-hydrophobic-core explanation remains an interpretation. The deletion is not restricted to PF01493, and the unaffected delta7 is outside its match; neither result proves isolated-domain assembly function.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:Q05755"],"label":"Reported delta40 alpha construct rather than productive full-length alpha in the beta-His6 coproduction system","node_id":"gltb-delta40-coproduction","node_type":"PERTURBATION"},{"label":"Reported detectable alpha-polypeptide production in BL21(DE3)","node_id":"detectable-alpha-polypeptide","node_type":"PHENOTYPE"}],"scope":"A. brasilense gltB C-terminal truncation coexpressed with His6-tagged beta in E. coli BL21(DE3), as reported in Cottevieille 2008; an expression phenotype, not directly measured folding failure.","scope_status":"PHENOTYPIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:192","title":"The delta40 alpha construct lacks detectable production in the reported expression attempts"}],"characterization_status":"UNSCORED","counters":{"alphafold_models":1560,"domain_architectures":158,"matches":21244,"proteins":21023,"proteomes":17485,"structures":13,"taxa":27304},"curation_events":[{"action":"CREATE","curator":"Codex","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF01493/2026-10-11T105840Z-codex-e03f25.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"outcome":"changed","summary":"Curated scoped GltS assembly and truncation graphs for PF01493.","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:58:40Z"},{"action":"REVIEW","curator":"Codex","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF01493/2026-10-11T110713Z-codex-6f6ef9.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"outcome":"needs_followup","summary":"Retained partial GltS assembly and expression scientific self-review.","timestamp":"2026-10-11T11:07:13Z"}],"curation_history":"history/records/PF01493","curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","description":"This domain is found in glutamate synthase, tungsten formylmethanofuran dehydrogenase subunit c (FwdC) and molybdenum formylmethanofuran dehydrogenase subunit c (FmdC). A repeated G-XX-G-XXX-G motif is seen in the alignment.","discussions":[{"discussion_id":"gxgxg-domain-boundaries-and-assembly-causality","evidence":[{"evidence_source":"full_text_and_supplement","explanation":"Main assembly/kinetic Results, relevant Methods/Discussion and supplemental construction/DLS information were inspected. Figure S3 and Table 2 were visually checked. Salt preincubation, assay salt and oligomer composition are not interchangeable interventions; the kinetic correlation and structural electron-transfer scheme are not adopted as observed domain-specific edges.","reference":"PMID:18199747","supports":"PARTIAL"},{"evidence_source":"deposited_sequence","explanation":"Exact polymer-reference matching resolves precursor versus mature numbering but does not reconstruct every later assay construct or prove a folding mechanism.","reference":"https://files.rcsb.org/download/1EA0.cif","supports":"SUPPORT"}],"kind":"CURA